1
00:00:02,116 --> 00:00:04,664
The quicksort algorithm certainly was an

2
00:00:04,664 --> 00:00:06,989
improvement over the bubble sort algorithm.

3
00:00:07,550 --> 00:00:10,740
After all, in the best and most importantly

4
00:00:10,996 --> 00:00:14,106
in the average case, we are able to achieve

5
00:00:14,154 --> 00:00:17,248
a time complexity of n times logarithm of n,

6
00:00:17,889 --> 00:00:20,198
which is better than O.

7
00:00:21,416 --> 00:00:24,366
Yet we have that worst case with that

8
00:00:24,398 --> 00:00:26,049
quadratic time complexity.

9
00:00:26,706 --> 00:00:28,805
Now maybe we can do better than that.

10
00:00:29,366 --> 00:00:31,593
Well, indeed we will be able to do better

11
00:00:31,593 --> 00:00:33,644
than that, and the reason for that is this

12
00:00:33,692 --> 00:00:36,497
pivot element which we use here in the

13
00:00:36,497 --> 00:00:39,701
quicksort algorithm. We always chose the

14
00:00:39,701 --> 00:00:42,425
first element, and in the worst case where

15
00:00:42,425 --> 00:00:45,518
we have a sorted array, that is a problem

16
00:00:45,934 --> 00:00:49,780
because then we always have one large array

17
00:00:49,876 --> 00:00:52,344
and one empty array. I talked about this in

18
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:53,129
the last lectures.

19
00:00:53,803 --> 00:00:55,971
That means that we don't really split the

20
00:00:55,971 --> 00:00:58,684
problem into smaller chunks and hence we

21
00:00:58,765 --> 00:01:00,756
don't get that better time complexity.

22
00:01:01,510 --> 00:01:04,240
That leads us to the merge sort algorithm,

23
00:01:04,705 --> 00:01:07,820
an algorithm which is also all about sorting

24
00:01:07,917 --> 00:01:09,249
a list, sorting an array,

25
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:11,963
but it will give us a better time

26
00:01:12,027 --> 00:01:14,901
complexity. I can already spoil that to you.

27
00:01:15,463 --> 00:01:18,016
Now, how does the merge sort algorithm do

28
00:01:18,032 --> 00:01:18,145
that?

29
00:01:19,172 --> 00:01:22,462
With the merge sort algorithm, we split the

30
00:01:22,462 --> 00:01:24,035
array multiple times

31
00:01:24,789 --> 00:01:25,897
and always in the middle

32
00:01:26,699 --> 00:01:29,315
until we have only 2-element arrays left. So

33
00:01:29,363 --> 00:01:31,947
we split this array into multiple 2-element

34
00:01:31,947 --> 00:01:33,825
arrays, and we'll do that recursively,

35
00:01:34,001 --> 00:01:35,446
always by splitting in the middle.

36
00:01:36,344 --> 00:01:38,960
And then we sort those arrays and we merge

37
00:01:38,992 --> 00:01:41,303
them back together. So here's how that will

38
00:01:41,384 --> 00:01:41,737
look like.

39
00:01:42,443 --> 00:01:43,165
We got this array

40
00:01:43,871 --> 00:01:46,359
and we split it once. In the middle. And if

41
00:01:46,359 --> 00:01:48,814
we have no perfect middle like here, well

42
00:01:48,943 --> 00:01:51,495
then close to the middle. So that in this

43
00:01:51,495 --> 00:01:54,079
case we have one 3 and one 4 element array.

44
00:01:54,624 --> 00:01:56,647
Now that's not the 2 element array I'm

45
00:01:56,711 --> 00:01:59,006
looking for, so we split this again

46
00:01:59,375 --> 00:02:02,200
recursively. We call that splitting or that

47
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,419
sorting function again.

48
00:02:04,254 --> 00:02:07,640
Hence we end up with these arrays here. We

49
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:10,080
got a couple of arrays with only 2 elements

50
00:02:10,192 --> 00:02:12,855
and one array with one element, that won't

51
00:02:12,855 --> 00:02:13,657
be a problem though.

52
00:02:14,459 --> 00:02:17,072
So now we split everything the way we want,

53
00:02:17,329 --> 00:02:18,916
always in the middle, and we got these

54
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:21,610
unsorted 2-element arrays.

55
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:25,892
The next step is that we now focus on those

56
00:02:26,309 --> 00:02:27,174
2-element arrays

57
00:02:27,832 --> 00:02:30,638
and we sort them. So in every 2-element

58
00:02:30,638 --> 00:02:33,428
array, we sort the items and only inside of

59
00:02:33,524 --> 00:02:34,583
that 2-element array.

60
00:02:35,705 --> 00:02:39,201
Now once we did that, we'll merge the arrays

61
00:02:39,378 --> 00:02:40,149
back together,

62
00:02:40,743 --> 00:02:42,685
hence the name merge sort.

63
00:02:43,247 --> 00:02:45,655
We merge these arrays back together.

64
00:02:46,378 --> 00:02:49,428
Now important, we merge them by keeping the

65
00:02:49,492 --> 00:02:52,285
order in mind. We don't just concatenate

66
00:02:52,478 --> 00:02:55,400
these 2 element arrays together. We didn't

67
00:02:55,432 --> 00:02:58,193
just concatenate the array with the 3 inside

68
00:02:58,193 --> 00:03:00,698
of it with the array with -3 and 10.

69
00:03:01,292 --> 00:03:02,833
Otherwise, we would have gotten an array

70
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:06,172
that has the element 3, -3, 10. No, instead,

71
00:03:06,204 --> 00:03:08,292
when we combined these 2 arrays in the

72
00:03:08,356 --> 00:03:10,780
bottom left corner here, we did that with

73
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:13,783
some extra logic that merged them into one

74
00:03:13,831 --> 00:03:16,448
array where the items are then ordered

75
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:19,081
correctly inside of that array too. So if

76
00:03:19,114 --> 00:03:21,040
you want to look at it like this, we

77
00:03:21,056 --> 00:03:22,855
actually have 2 steps in that whole

78
00:03:23,047 --> 00:03:25,359
algorithm where we sort things.

79
00:03:25,953 --> 00:03:28,506
We sort, we order the things in the

80
00:03:28,603 --> 00:03:29,694
2-element arrays,

81
00:03:30,353 --> 00:03:32,664
and then When we merge all these arrays

82
00:03:32,776 --> 00:03:36,049
together again, we again watch out for the

83
00:03:36,129 --> 00:03:38,776
order and we again have some logic to order

84
00:03:38,872 --> 00:03:39,754
things correctly.

85
00:03:40,557 --> 00:03:42,851
And of course, we then do this one more time

86
00:03:43,188 --> 00:03:45,546
to merge this all into one big array and

87
00:03:45,610 --> 00:03:49,268
it's based on this branch of subarrays which

88
00:03:49,364 --> 00:03:52,877
we built temporarily during our process.

89
00:03:53,968 --> 00:03:58,208
So that's the merge sort algorithm. We split

90
00:03:58,208 --> 00:04:00,838
things up, we sort them, and we also sort

91
00:04:00,935 --> 00:04:03,388
things when we then merge the arrays back

92
00:04:03,469 --> 00:04:03,888
together.

93
00:04:04,582 --> 00:04:07,132
Now let's have a look at that in action.
